  "aiSummary": "This resolution formally adopts the permanent operating rules for the North Carolina State Senate for the 2025 legislative session. The rules cover procedures for debate, voting, committee operations, bill handling, and general parliamentary conduct that will govern how the Senate functions during the session.",
  "aiProArguments": "Supporters argue that established parliamentary rules provide necessary structure and predictability for the legislative process. These rules protect minority rights through procedures like two-thirds vote requirements for certain actions, ensure transparency through public committee meetings and recorded votes, and create fair processes for bill consideration so that legislative business proceeds in an orderly manner.",
  "aiConArguments": "Critics might argue that rigid procedural rules can slow down the legislative process or concentrate power in leadership roles like the President Pro Tempore, who has significant discretion over bill referrals and calendar management. Some rules about deadlines and voting procedures could be seen as limiting flexibility to respond to emergencies or last-minute issues during the session.",
